================================================================================
MODELS
================================================================================

bert-base-uncased
  Copyright The Google AI Language Team Authors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/google-bert/bert-base-uncased
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

  Modifications: two derivative models were produced from this checkpoint.
    1. Tweet sentiment — all 109,484,547 parameters fine-tuned for 3 epochs
       (AdamW, lr 5e-5, batch 16, max_length 128) with a 3-class head replacing
       the pre-training head.
    2. Movie review sentiment — base weights frozen; a LoRA adapter (rank 8,
       alpha 32, dropout 0.1, applied to the query and value projections of
       every attention layer) and a 2-class head were trained, together 297,988
       parameters, 0.27% of the network.

torchvision ResNet-18, ImageNet-pretrained weights (ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT)
  Copyright (c) Soumith Chintala 2016, and the PyTorch contributors.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  https://github.com/pytorch/vision

  Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
  modification, are permitted provided that the conditions of the BSD 3-Clause
  License are met. THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND
  CONTRIBUTORS "AS IS" AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES ARE DISCLAIMED.

  Modifications: the final fully-connected layer was replaced with a 2-way
  linear head and the network fine-tuned for 10 epochs (Adam, lr 1e-4, weight
  decay 1e-4, batch 32) with horizontal flips, +/-10 degree rotation and colour
  jitter, on a seeded stratified split.

================================================================================
DATASETS
================================================================================

None of the datasets below are redistributed in this repository. See
scripts/get_data.py for how to obtain each from its original source.

Tweet Sentiment Extraction
  https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/tweet-sentiment-extraction
  Subject to the Kaggle competition rules, which permit use for "academic
  research and education, and other non-commercial purposes" and state: "You
  agree not to transmit, duplicate, publish, redistribute or otherwise provide
  or make available the Data to any party not participating in the Competition."

  Accordingly this repository contains no tweet corpus, and no per-prediction
  records for that task -- those reproduce the text in bulk. Aggregate
  statistics derived from the corpus are included, as are three tweets quoted
  as worked examples in the report.

Counterfactually-Augmented Data (IMDb movie reviews)
  Kaushik, D., Hovy, E., & Lipton, Z. C. (2020). Learning the Difference that
  Makes a Difference with Counterfactually-Augmented Data. ICLR.
  https://github.com/acmi-lab/counterfactually-augmented-data
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Saliency-Bench (glasses detection images and human attention masks)
  Zhang, Y., et al. (2025). Saliency-Bench: A Comprehensive Benchmark for
  Evaluating Visual Explanations. arXiv:2310.08537.
  https://xaidataset.github.io/

  No licence is stated by the authors at the time of writing. The images and
  attention masks are therefore not redistributed here, and the per-prediction
  records for this task contain file paths and numerical attributions only.

